Fixed CPU query
fetch dt.entity.host
| filter arrayIndexOf(tags, "APMID:APP00005497") != -1
| fields id, hostname = entity.name

| join [
    timeseries cpu = avg(dt.host.cpu.usage, scalar:true), by:{dt.entity.host}
  ], kind:leftOuter, on: left[id] == right[dt.entity.host]
| fieldsAdd cpu_avg_pct = round(right.cpu, decimals:2)

| filter cpu_avg_pct >= 10
| fields hostname, cpu_avg_pct
| sort cpu_avg_pct desc

What changed
Added scalar:true inside the avg() aggregation itself — this computes one true average value per host directly from the raw data points, rather than averaging a series of already-averaged time buckets.
Since the result is now already a single scalar (not an array), dropped arrayAvg() entirely — just reference right.cpu directly.
Same fix needed for Memory query
